<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP dependency-check suppression file (AAP §0.7.8 — "zero critical/high CVE"
  gate; the finding's resolution explicitly permits "any valid suppressions only
  if justified"). Every entry below is a documented CPE/scope FALSE POSITIVE or a
  not-applicable-to-this-closure match: dependency-check matched a shared CPE to
  the wrong artifact, or to a module that is provably absent from the resolved
  dependency tree. No genuine vulnerability is suppressed.

  Scoping discipline:
    * Each <suppress> is scoped to the EXACT flagged artifact (packageUrl) AND the
      EXACT CVE(s). No blanket/product-wide suppressions are used.
    * packageUrl matches are version-agnostic (@.*$) so a future patch bump does
      not silently re-open the gate — but the CVE list stays pinned, so any NEW
      CVE on the same artifact still fails the build.
    * Evidence for each rationale was verified against `mvn dependency:tree` and
      the dependency-check JSON report (vulnerableSoftware CPE ranges) at the time
      of writing.

  Schema: https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

    <!-- =====================================================================
         org.eclipse.angus:angus-activation  —  CVE-2025-7962  (FALSE POSITIVE)
         =====================================================================
         CVE-2025-7962 is an SMTP-injection flaw in Jakarta/Angus *Mail* (the
         CPEs recorded by the NVD are cpe:2.3:a:eclipse:angus_mail [< 2.0.4] and
         cpe:2.3:a:eclipse:jakarta_mail [< 1.6.8; 2.0.0–2.0.2]). The flagged
         artifact, org.eclipse.angus:angus-activation, is the Jakarta *Activation*
         (JAF) implementation — a different product that merely shares the
         `org.eclipse.angus` Maven group, which dependency-check mis-mapped to the
         eclipse:angus_mail CPE. No mail artifact (angus-mail, jakarta.mail-api,
         com.sun.mail) is present in the resolved dependency tree, so the
         vulnerable Mail/SMTP code is not on the classpath. angus-activation has no
         SMTP capability and 2.0.3 is its current release (there is no "2.0.4"
         activation fix — that version refers to angus-mail). -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CPE false positive. CVE-2025-7962 affects Angus/Jakarta MAIL (SMTP
            injection), not the Jakarta ACTIVATION implementation. angus-activation
            shares the org.eclipse.angus group but contains no mail/SMTP code, and
            no mail artifact exists in the dependency tree (verified via
            dependency:tree). Suppressed for this CVE only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.eclipse\.angus/angus-activation@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2025-7962</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api  —  CVE-2026-34478 / -34479 /
         -34480 / -34481  (FALSE POSITIVE)
         =====================================================================
         All four CVEs are in Log4j *Core* layout classes:
           * CVE-2026-34478 — Rfc5424Layout
           * CVE-2026-34479 — Log4j1XmlLayout (Log4j 1.x bridge)
           * CVE-2026-34480 — XmlLayout
           * CVE-2026-34481 — JsonTemplateLayout
         These classes live exclusively in org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core.
         This application logs through SLF4J/Logback; the ONLY Log4j2 artifact on
         the classpath is the log4j-*api* facade (pulled transitively by
         log4j-to-slf4j to route any Log4j2 API calls into SLF4J). log4j-core is
         ABSENT from the dependency tree (verified via dependency:tree —
         only log4j-api and log4j-to-slf4j are present), so the vulnerable layout
         classes can never be loaded or executed. Scoped to log4j-api specifically:
         if log4j-core were ever added, these CVEs would correctly surface on it. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CPE false positive. CVE-2026-34478/-34479/-34480/-34481 are in Log4j
            CORE layout classes (Rfc5424/Log4j1Xml/Xml/JsonTemplate). Only the
            log4j-API facade is present (via log4j-to-slf4j -> SLF4J/Logback);
            log4j-core is absent from the dependency tree (verified). The
            vulnerable classes are not on the classpath. Scoped to log4j-api only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.logging\.log4j/log4j-api@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-34478</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-34479</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-34480</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-34481</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-prometheus  —  CVE-2026-42154
         (FALSE POSITIVE)
         =====================================================================
         CVE-2026-42154 is in the Prometheus *server* (the Go monitoring server,
         CPE cpe:2.3:a:prometheus:prometheus, affected < 3.5.3 and 3.6.0–3.11.3):
         its remote-read endpoint /api/v1/read mishandles input. The flagged
         artifact, io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-prometheus 1.15.x, is the
         Micrometer Java CLIENT library that merely EXPOSES application metrics in
         Prometheus exposition format; it is not the Prometheus server and ships no
         /api/v1/read endpoint. The product and version lines do not even overlap
         (Micrometer 1.15.x vs Prometheus-server 3.x). dependency-check mis-mapped
         the "prometheus" token to the prometheus:prometheus CPE. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CPE false positive. CVE-2026-42154 affects the Prometheus Go SERVER
            (/api/v1/read remote-read endpoint). This artifact is the Micrometer
            Java CLIENT registry that exposes metrics in Prometheus format; it is
            not the server and has no such endpoint. Suppressed for this CVE only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.micrometer/micrometer-registry-prometheus@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-42154</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         io.netty:netty-transport  —  CVE-2026-42582  (NOT APPLICABLE)
         =====================================================================
         Per the authoritative Netty 4.2.13.Final release notes, CVE-2026-42582 is
         a flaw in netty-codec-*http3* (non-Huffman header-block decode). That
         HTTP/3 codec module is a 4.2.x-line component and is ABSENT from this
         closure — the only HTTP codec present is netty-codec-http2 (verified via
         dependency:tree; no netty-codec-http3 / http3 / quic artifact resolves).
         The NVD CPE for this CVE (cpe:2.3:a:netty:netty, versionEndExcluding
         4.2.13 with NO lower bound) therefore over-matches the entire 4.1.x line,
         landing on netty-transport 4.1.135.Final purely by shared product CPE.

         netty here is used only CLIENT-side by the AWS SDK v2 netty-nio-client
         (software.amazon.awssdk:netty-nio-client, via spring-cloud-aws S3/SQS/SNS)
         to call trusted AWS / LocalStack endpoints; the application's own HTTP
         server is embedded Tomcat, not netty. The published fix is Netty 4.2.13,
         but Netty 4.1 and 4.2 cannot share a classpath and 4.2.x requires Spring
         Boot 4.x — a major-version migration outside the Minimal Change Clause
         (§0.7.1). netty is already pinned to the latest 4.1.x patch (4.1.135.Final)
         via the netty-bom override in pom.xml, which resolves the genuine 4.1.x
         CVEs. Because the over-broad netty:netty CPE matches EVERY io.netty
         module at 4.1.135 (dependency-check assigns CVE-2026-42582 to
         netty-transport, netty-transport-classes-epoll, and potentially other
         netty-* jars sharing that CPE), this suppression is scoped to all
         io.netty modules — but ONLY for this single CVE. None of the modules on
         the classpath is netty-codec-http3, so the vulnerable code is absent. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Not applicable to this closure. CVE-2026-42582 is in netty-codec-http3
            (4.2.x line); that module is ABSENT (only netty-codec-http2 present,
            verified). The NVD CPE lacks a lower bound and over-matches 4.1.x. netty
            is pinned to the latest 4.1.x patch (4.1.135.Final) and used client-side
            only against trusted AWS/LocalStack endpoints (app server is Tomcat). The
            fix (4.2.13) needs Netty 4.2.x + Spring Boot 4.x, outside the Minimal
            Change Clause. The over-broad netty:netty CPE matches multiple io.netty
            modules (netty-transport, netty-transport-classes-epoll, ...); scoped to
            all io.netty modules for THIS CVE only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.netty/.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-42582</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         io.opentelemetry.semconv:opentelemetry-semconv  —  CVE-2026-39882 /
         CVE-2026-39883  (FALSE POSITIVE)
         =====================================================================
         Both CVEs are in OpenTelemetry-*Go* (the Go SDK), whose NVD CPE explicitly
         targets the `go` platform
         (cpe:2.3:a:opentelemetry:opentelemetry:*:*:*:*:*:go:*:*):
           * CVE-2026-39882 — the otlp HTTP exporters (traces/metrics/logs) read
             the full HTTP response body into an unbounded in-memory bytes.Buffer
             (Go memory-exhaustion); fixed in OpenTelemetry-Go 1.43.0.
           * CVE-2026-39883 — incomplete fix of CVE-2026-24051; changed a Darwin
             `ioreg` command invocation (Go), range 1.15.0–1.43.0.
         The flagged artifact, io.opentelemetry.semconv:opentelemetry-semconv, is a
         Java jar of GENERATED semantic-convention constants (String/AttributeKey
         definitions) with no HTTP exporter, no `bytes.Buffer`, no command
         execution, and no platform-specific code at all. The match is purely the
         shared "opentelemetry" product token across two different language
         ecosystems (Go vs Java). Scoped to this artifact and these two CVEs only. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CPE false positive. CVE-2026-39882 (Go otlp HTTP exporter unbounded
            response buffer) and CVE-2026-39883 (Go Darwin `ioreg` command) both
            affect OpenTelemetry-GO; the CPE targets the `go` platform. This is a
            Java constants jar with no exporter/command/platform code. Suppressed
            for these two CVEs only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/io\.opentelemetry\.semconv/opentelemetry-semconv@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-39882</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-39883</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api  —  CVE-2025-68161 / CVE-2026-34477
         (FALSE POSITIVE)
         =====================================================================
         Both CVEs are in the Log4j *Core* SocketAppender / SslConfiguration:
           * CVE-2025-68161 — the Socket Appender in Apache Log4j Core
             (2.0-beta9 .. 2.25.2) skips TLS hostname verification of the peer
             certificate even when verifyHostName / log4j2.sslVerifyHostName is set.
           * CVE-2026-34477 — the incomplete fix of CVE-2025-68161 (the <Ssl>
             verifyHostName attribute path remained unverified).
         The SocketAppender and its SslConfiguration live exclusively in
         org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core. This application logs through
         SLF4J/Logback; the ONLY Log4j2 artifact on the classpath is the
         log4j-*api* facade (pulled transitively by log4j-to-slf4j to route any
         Log4j2 API calls into SLF4J). log4j-core is ABSENT from the dependency
         tree (verified via dependency:tree — only log4j-api and log4j-to-slf4j
         are present), so the SocketAppender code can never be loaded, configured,
         or executed, and the application opens no Log4j network/TLS socket at all.
         Scoped to log4j-api specifically: if log4j-core were ever added, these
         CVEs would correctly surface on it. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CPE false positive. CVE-2025-68161 and CVE-2026-34477 are in the Log4j
            CORE SocketAppender / SslConfiguration (TLS hostname verification).
            Only the log4j-API facade is present (via log4j-to-slf4j -> SLF4J/
            Logback); log4j-core is absent from the dependency tree (verified), so
            the SocketAppender is not on the classpath. Scoped to log4j-api only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.logging\.log4j/log4j-api@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2025-68161</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-34477</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         org.hibernate.validator:hibernate-validator  —  CVE-2025-15104
         (FALSE POSITIVE)
         =====================================================================
         CVE-2025-15104 is a restriction-bypass (DNS-rebinding SSRF) in "The Nu
         Html Checker (vnu / validator.nu)" — an HTML-validation web service. Its
         NVD CPE is cpe:2.3:a:validator:validator:*. The flagged artifact,
         org.hibernate.validator:hibernate-validator 8.0.3.Final, is the Jakarta
         Bean Validation (JSR 380) reference implementation — a completely
         different product that merely shares the generic "validator" token, which
         dependency-check mis-mapped to the validator:validator CPE. Hibernate
         Validator performs in-JVM constraint validation of bean fields; it issues
         no outbound HTTP/HTTPS requests and exposes no hostname-protection control
         that could be bypassed. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            CPE false positive. CVE-2025-15104 affects the Nu Html Checker
            (validator.nu) HTML-validation service (CPE validator:validator), not
            the Hibernate Validator Jakarta Bean Validation engine. Hibernate
            Validator makes no outbound HTTP requests. Suppressed for this CVE only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.hibernate\.validator/hibernate-validator@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2025-15104</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib  —  CVE-2020-29582  (ALREADY PATCHED)
         =====================================================================
         CVE-2020-29582 affects "JetBrains Kotlin *before 1.4.21*" — a vulnerable
         Java temp-file/temp-folder API (insecure default permissions allowing
         local information disclosure). It was fixed in Kotlin 1.4.21. The flagged
         artifact, org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib 1.9.25, is FIVE minor
         versions past the fix and is NOT vulnerable; it is present only
         transitively (no application Kotlin code exists). dependency-check matched
         the jetbrains:kotlin product CPE without honoring the < 1.4.21 upper bound,
         so the match over-reaches the patched 1.9.x line. The shared jetbrains:kotlin
         CPE lands on BOTH resolved Kotlin modules — kotlin-stdlib 1.9.25 and its
         companion kotlin-stdlib-jdk7 1.9.25 — so the packageUrl below is scoped to
         all kotlin-stdlib* artifacts, but ONLY for this single CVE; a future Kotlin
         CVE on the same jars would still surface. -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
            Already patched / version over-match. CVE-2020-29582 was fixed in
            Kotlin 1.4.21; the resolved artifacts are kotlin-stdlib 1.9.25 and
            kotlin-stdlib-jdk7 1.9.25 (>> 1.4.21) and are not vulnerable. Present
            transitively only (no Kotlin app code). The CPE match ignores the
            < 1.4.21 upper bound and hits both stdlib modules. Scoped to all
            kotlin-stdlib* artifacts for this CVE only.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/kotlin-stdlib.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2020-29582</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>
